# The Coxeter number and the Coxeter element that carries it. Every simple Lie algebra has a rank, the number of simple
# roots, and a Coxeter number h, and these fix its size: the count of roots is the rank times the Coxeter number, and the
# dimension is the roots plus the rank. So E8, of rank eight and Coxeter number thirty, has eight times thirty, two
# hundred forty roots, and dimension two hundred forty-eight. The Coxeter number is the order of the Coxeter element, the
# product of all the simple reflections, which permutes the roots in one long cycle. For the rank-two algebra A2 the
# Coxeter number is three and the Coxeter element rotates its three positive roots in a three-cycle. This file MODELS the
# three roots of A2 and DEFINES the Coxeter element as the rotation through them, then PROVES it has order three, applying
# it three times returns every root, so the Coxeter number of A2 is three. The E8 root count and dimension are recorded as
# machine-integer facts. The order theorem is proved over the actual root type by induction.

# The three positive roots of the rank-two algebra A2, permuted by its Coxeter element.
form a-two-root
  case alpha
  case beta
  case gamma

# The Coxeter element of A2, the product of its simple reflections, rotating the three roots in one cycle.
task coxeter-element
  take r, like a-two-root
  like a-two-root
  fork case, read r
    case alpha
      send back
        make beta
    case beta
      send back
        make gamma
    case gamma
      send back
        make alpha

# THE COXETER ELEMENT HAS ORDER THREE: applying it three times returns every root, coxeter-element applied thrice is the
# identity, for every root. So the Coxeter number of A2 is three, the order of its Coxeter element. Proved by induction
# over the three roots.
rule the-coxeter-element-has-order-three
  seat r, like a-two-root
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call coxeter-element
        call coxeter-element
          call coxeter-element
            read r
      read r
  fold r

# IT IS NOT THE IDENTITY at one step: the Coxeter element sends alpha to beta, not back to alpha, so its order is exactly
# three and not one.
rule the-coxeter-element-moves-alpha
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call coxeter-element
        make alpha
      make beta
  calm hold

# THE E8 ROOT COUNT as a machine-integer fact: rank eight times Coxeter number thirty is two hundred forty roots,
# 8 * 30 = 240, the E8 kissing number.
hold e-eight-has-two-hundred-forty-roots
  call is-equal
    code 240
    call multiply
      code 8
      code 30

# THE E8 DIMENSION is the roots plus the rank, 240 + 8 = 248, which is also rank eight times the Coxeter number plus one,
# 8 * 31.
hold e-eight-dimension-is-two-hundred-forty-eight
  call is-equal
    code 248
    call multiply
      code 8
      code 31
